      "role": "supplementary",
      "technique": "Confocal laser scanning microscopy (reflection mode Z-stacking)",
      "why": "An upright confocal microscope can accommodate opaque implants and capture 3D Z-stacks in reflected-light mode to approximate coarse micron-scale topography; however, biological confocal systems have limited axial resolution (~0.5–1 µm) and are not metrologically calibrated for standard surface roughness parameters.",
      "accessories_to_confirm": [
        "Reflected-light (backscatter) detection mode configuration",
        "High-numerical-aperture dry (air) metallurgical/materiallographic objective",
        "3D surface topography / roughness analysis software module"
