      "role": "supplementary",
      "technique": "Confocal and multiphoton laser scanning microscopy",
      "why": "If a fluorescent dye is infiltrated into marginal gaps, optical sectioning can trace gap morphology to a shallow depth (typically up to a few hundred micrometers), but light scattering in enamel, dentin, and composite prevents imaging deep inside an intact tooth.",
      "accessories_to_confirm": [
        "Long-working-distance objectives suitable for whole tooth topography",
        "Stage insert capable of holding an intact extracted tooth"
      ]
    },
    {
      "instrument_id": "EQ14",
      "role": "supplementary",
      "technique": "Stereomicroscopy",
      "why": "Provides low-magnification inspection of external restoration margins and surface defects on an intact tooth, though it cannot reveal subsurface voids or internal interfacial gaps.",
