  "summary": "No instrument on the equipment list can non-destructively image the deep interior of an intact tooth to check for internal voids and gaps. Accomplishing this without cutting the tooth requires X-ray micro-computed tomography (micro-CT) or optical coherence tomography (OCT), which are not listed. Among the available instruments, ESEM (EQ10) and stereomicroscopy (EQ14) can only inspect external surface margins on an uncut tooth, while multiphoton/confocal microscopy (EQ08) can only probe shallow subsurface gaps if a fluorescent tracer dye is used."
}

{
