      "role": "supplementary",
      "technique": "Environmental scanning electron microscopy (ESEM)",
      "why": "If low-magnification optical inspection reveals fine cracks or layer-delamination defects that need closer examination, ESEM can image fine surface topography on non-conductive resin parts without requiring a conductive coating, provided the parts fit inside the sample chamber.",
