  "clarifying_question": null,
  "summary": "For fast, low-magnification inspection of resin-printed parts for cracks, warping, and missing features, the Nikon SMZ 445 stereomicroscope (EQ14) is the primary tool because it offers a wide field of view and large working distance for three-dimensional objects. If you need higher-magnification follow-up on fine fracture surfaces or layer defects, the Philips XL30 ESEM (EQ10) can image uncoated resin parts that fit its chamber. If you eventually need quantitative 3D warpage maps against your CAD file or internal defect detection, 3D optical scanning or micro-CT would be required, which are not on the equipment list."
}

